"""Part G tool teaching records — batch t3 (ten tools).

Written to agree with src/tool_catalogue.json (age, measures, cannot-tell-you,
time, lands-in), Reference Part A ('Phonological and literacy measures',
'Behavioural and emotional rating scales'), Part D (rows 507–650) and the
Skill progression phonological micro-skills (CTOPP-2 citation).
No norms, cut-offs, reliability figures, item counts or subtest lists are
stated as fact unless well established; elsewhere the entry says
'check the manual'. PLS-5 and Renfrew are usually SLT instruments in Irish
practice — the entries say what the EP does with an SLT's result.
"""

